{#
  VTEP addresses for EVPN.

  OVN-Kubernetes allocates each node a VXLAN tunnel endpoint address out of
  these CIDRs and puts it on a dummy interface. The fabric learns those
  addresses as the next hops for every EVPN route, so the block has to be
  routable from the fabric - which it is, because the nodes advertise it over
  the existing default-VRF session to leaf1.

  Deliberately a block that exists nowhere else in this lab: not
  {{ lab_network_prefix }}.0/24, not {{ clab_fabric_prefix }}.0/24, not any
  tenant prefix. A VTEP address that collides with a real one produces
  tunnels that form and then carry traffic to the wrong place.
#}
apiVersion: k8s.ovn.org/v1
kind: VTEP
metadata:
  name: evpn-vtep
spec:
  cidrs:
    - 100.64.0.0/24
  mode: managed
